parameters.jsCode:
// Normalize the submitted form into the single shape the rest of the workflow expects.
// Form Trigger fields arrive as JSON keys named by their labels; a webhook-style
// payload would arrive under "body". Both are accepted so the node stays reusable.
// No completeness check here: every form field is required, so the Form Trigger
// has already rejected anything missing before it reaches this node.
const items = $input.all();
const out = [];

const EMAIL_PATTERN = /[A-Za-z0-9._%+\-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.\-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}/;
const firstEmail = (text) => {
  const match = EMAIL_PATTERN.exec(String(text || ''));
  return match ? match[0] : '';
};

for (const item of items) {
  const raw = item.json || {};
  const body = (raw.body && typeof raw.body === 'object') ? raw.body : raw;

  const pick = (...values) => {
    for (const value of values) {
      const text = String(value ?? '').trim();
      if (text) return text;
    }
    return '';
  };

  // The form's first field is "Name", so the pipeline calls it name throughout
  // (older payloads that sent "Name or Email" / "sender" are still accepted).
  const name    = pick(body['Name'], body.name, body['Name or Email'], body.sender);
  const subject = pick(body['Subject'], body.subject, body.topic);
  const message = pick(body['Message'], body.message, body.text);
  const submittedAt = pick(body.submittedAt, '');

  // The address the reply goes to: the Email field first, then anything that
  // looks like an address in the name field or the message body.
  const email = pick(
    body['Email'],
    body.email,
    firstEmail(body['Name or Email']),
    firstEmail(name),
    firstEmail(message),
  );

  // Stable id: the same submission always hashes the same, so a retry upserts
  // onto the existing log row instead of creating a duplicate.
  const fingerprint = (text) => {
    let hash = 5381;
    for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) hash = ((hash * 33) ^ text.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0;
    return hash.toString(16).toUpperCase().padStart(8, '0');
  };
  const messageId = 'MSG-' + fingerprint([name, subject, message, submittedAt || String(Date.now())].join('|'));

  out.push({
    json: {
      name,
      email,
      subject,
      message,
      submitted_at: submittedAt || null,
      message_id: messageId,
      received_at: new Date().toISOString(),
    },
  });
}

return out;

parameters.text:
=You write the reply email for the College of the Desert CIS Department support inbox.

Voice: warm, professional and upbeat. Every sentence must be complete and properly punctuated. Never use bullet points, headings, or sentence fragments.

Sender:
- Name: {{ $('Format').first().json.name }}
- Subject: {{ $('Format').first().json.subject }}
- Message: {{ $('Format').first().json.message }}

Triage:
- Category: {{ $('Classify Message').first().json.output.category }}
- Confidence: {{ $('Classify Message').first().json.output.confidence }}
- Reasoning: {{ $('Classify Message').first().json.output.reasoning }}

Knowledge base answer (the only facts you may use):
{{ $json.kb_answer || 'NO KNOWLEDGE BASE ENTRY MATCHED THIS MESSAGE.' }}

Knowledge base matches (id:category:question:score): {{ $('Search Knowledge Base').first().json.kb_matches.map(m => m.id + ':' + m.category + ':' + m.question + ':' + m.score).join(' | ') }}

Rules:
1. Use only the knowledge base answer above. Never invent facts, names, dates, or policies. If it does not answer the question, say the message has been passed to the CIS Department to follow up.
2. If the sender named a specific course (for example CIS 091), answer only about that course and leave out the other courses the knowledge base answer lists.
3. For an instructor question, phrase it exactly like this: "The professor for CIS 091 is Patrick Jacobs." Never write "CIS 091 is Patrick Jacobs."
4. Layout: greet the sender by first name, thank them for reaching out in one upbeat sentence, give the answer, add one friendly closing line that invites a reply, then sign off with "Warm regards," and "CIS Department Support" on separate lines.
5. Set needs_human_review to true when the knowledge base has no answer, confidence is below 0.6, the knowledge base category disagrees with the triage category, or the knowledge base does not cover the course the sender asked about. Otherwise set it to false.
6. Never mention the knowledge base, the classification, confidence scores, or that you are an AI.

Return only the structured output.
